menu "mini scope"

config MINI_SCOPE_SAMPLE_RATE
    int "Sample rate (Hz)"
    default 200000
    help
        Sampling rate in samples per second.  The I²S driver uses this
        to configure the ADC sampling clock.  Higher rates reduce
        available UART throughput and increase noise.

config MINI_SCOPE_FRAME_SAMPLES
    int "Frame size (samples)"
    default 1024
    help
        Number of samples per frame.  Determines how many samples
        are read from I²S before a frame is sent.  Larger frames
        increase latency but reduce protocol overhead.

config MINI_SCOPE_ADC_GAIN
    float "ADC gain correction"
    default 1.0
    help
        Multiplicative correction applied to raw ADC counts before
        they are transmitted.  Adjust this to calibrate front‑end
        attenuation or op‑amp gain.

config MINI_SCOPE_ADC_OFFSET
    int "ADC offset correction (counts)"
    default 0
    help
        Additive correction applied to raw ADC counts.  Useful to
        compensate for DC offsets from the bias network or op‑amp.

endmenu